  "comment": "kiln.hooks typed links (dev.28, chapter 06b): two new symbols and the descriptors (\"sigs\") of the ten functions a mod can hook or call as functions. A descriptor lists the declared parameters only; a struct returned through a hidden buffer is \"sret\". \"abi\" is the function's fingerprint on the builds this file was checked against (tools/sigport/sigdb_check.py --fptool); the core compares it with the code at load and turns sig/<symbol> off when they differ. \"invoke\" says whether a direct call is offered (none, tick = tick thread only, any). Shared with the client (the fingerprints are the same on both exes). Evidence: docs/re/systems.",
